  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through Thursday)\nIssued at 1232 AM CST Fri Nov 6 2026\n\nBy Saturday night most place across our CWA will be experiencing \nrain showers or just steady rain. As moisture continues to stream \ntogether from the Gulf and the shortwave (cutoff low) that \neventually looks to transition into a coastal low. Eventually this \nCoastal low looks to push off to the southeast taking all the \nmoisture and rain chances with it. Right now the highest chances for \nseeing beneficial rains will be wherever the low-level and mid-level \nmoisture streams overlap the most. This currently includes areas \nalong the Rio Grande eastward towards the San Antonio area, with \nareas further north and east such as the austin metro area seeing \nless rain chances. This is because most models are hinting at low \nlevel moisture decreasing as the coastal low pushes further south \nand east throughout the weekend. Amounts look relatively healthy \nwith many seeing totals in the 2 to 4 inch range with almost everyone \nseeing at least a half inch to an inch when all is said an done. \nThese totals may seem like a lot but we arent expecting any heavy \ntorrential downpours but rather some good old fashioned steady cool \nrain that will occur over a period of several days rather than all \nat once. That being said recent model runs have locked in on this \ncoastal low sticking around slightly longer and we may see rain \nchances continue through monday afternoon before finally tapering \noff monday evening. \n\nAs far as highs go, with the steady rainfall and extensive cloud \ncover we may see some areas struggle to break out of the mid 50s for \nhighs with most remaining in the low to mid 60s. Lows however wont \ndrop off too much as the clouds should keep most of the area fairly \ninsulated and prevent any radiational cooling form happening with \nmost staying in the upper 40s to near 50 degrees. Beyond Monday as \nwe begin to dry out we should see highs rebound back near 70 for \nTuesday with temps well into the 70s to round out the end of the \nweek along with lows remaining in the 50s.",
